{
  "//": "Election-COS1.0 — project electioncos1-0 (project number 960903975002, display name 'Election-COS'). Changed from election2026-campaignms7-0 on 28 Oct 2026, confirmed four ways: the console Project info card, the GCP dashboard analysis, an authenticated Cloud Shell prompt, and the deploy log. Region is settled — 'gcloud firestore databases list' returns the (default) database in africa-south1, FIRESTORE_NATIVE, and 'gcloud app describe' reports no App Engine application, so nothing pinned the location elsewhere. See docs/asset-control-sheet.md §28.",
  "projects": {
    "default": "electioncos1-0"
  },
  "//targets": "The 'app' target is the Hosting site serving app.electioncos.co.za — the PWA. It resolves to the project's default site, electioncos1-0, which is also what electioncos1-0.web.app serves and what publicDomain.ts carries as HOSTING_ORIGIN. The apex, electioncos.co.za, is NOT here: it is served from Cloudflare and is deliberately a different thing. Naming the target rather than relying on the default site is what makes 'firebase deploy --only hosting:app' mean something, and what keeps a second site from being deployed to by accident later.",
  "targets": {
    "electioncos1-0": {
      "hosting": {
        "app": [
          "electioncos1-0"
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
